+## Implementation task pack
+
+Task IM-AP-01; owner unassigned; status specified, implementation queued. Location boundary: src/kits/locations/apothecary/content, assets and sequences. Investigation owns mechanical progress and discovered evidence; Inventory owns items; Narrative owns choices/relationships; Campaign and Scene keep their existing completion/travel boundaries. Presentation owns control and cue descriptors. Dependencies: CAP-INPUT, CAP-MECHANISM, CAP-PROJECTION, CAP-SAVE and CAP-SEQUENCE. Physical controls and new logical state are proposed capabilities; current orisonOperations supports only observe/combine/use/dialogue/choose/solve/complete. Do not call new operation names or bypass source prerequisite checks as if they were installed.
+
+1. Read AP-01 and its source mapping. Load the actual apothecary incoming fixture; record current required clues and departure guard.
+2. Create the declared control definitions for sample-spoon, test-burner, sample-selector only after the shared input and state capabilities pass their tasks.
+3. Bind each exact action step to a validated Investigation transition. Place required clues in the authored scene before their observation receipts are possible.
+4. Project the accepted and blocked state changes through Presentation; use the listed procedural fallbacks until approved source assets exist.
+5. Coordinate finite completion via verified receipt waits; keep pressure inside Threat and do not put frame callbacks in a location Sequence.
+6. Commit existing source effects at the specified stage; preserve idempotency across reward, primary completion and departure.
+7. Implement the named restore and cancellation cases, then run the encounter and route acceptance walkthroughs from legal input.
+8. Attach source revision, observed behavior, screenshots and outstanding assets. Mark implemented only after these runtime gates pass.
+
