 Proposed Investigation-owned logical record: encounterId=SH-01, definitionVersion=1, confirmedStep (0 through 3), completed, and a validated control-value record keyed only by photo-pieces, seal-view, alias-tab. Decision records additionally store a preview selection separately from the single Narrative/Campaign commit. This is a proposed schema extension, not an existing installed API. Snapshot logical state plus owning-domain effects at one safe commit boundary. Never save DOM nodes, callbacks, drag pointers, audio handles, frame timestamps or an animation position as authority. On restore, reconstruct controls from confirmed state and replay only noncommitting feedback; never award a reward again. An interrupted unconfirmed drag/hold returns to its last stable detent. A wrong attempt resets only the local unsolved control sequence specified above; verified clues, items, primary completion and committed choices remain. Validate the whole snapshot and definition version before replacing any live owner; an unknown version leaves the current session unchanged. Entry/exit removes input subscriptions, stops local audio and cancels uncommitted operation receipts. Retry preserves original branch commitments and can always return to the named shelter.
 
+## Presentation and asset requests
+
+- `orison.design.sh-01.photo-pieces` — photo-pieces: place or select pairs. Place in the encounter’s named interaction zone with the clue reference visible from the same close view. Use the operation and obstruction described in action steps; do not substitute a decorative prop. Variants: idle, focused, blocked-with-reason, stable-after-action. Fallback: Labelled procedural proxy with the same shape/symbol and focus control; never remove its gameplay input..
+- `orison.design.sh-01.seal-view` — seal-view: enlarge matching marks. Place in the encounter’s named interaction zone with the clue reference visible from the same close view. Use the operation and obstruction described in action steps; do not substitute a decorative prop. Variants: idle, focused, blocked-with-reason, stable-after-action. Fallback: Labelled procedural proxy with the same shape/symbol and focus control; never remove its gameplay input..
+- `orison.design.sh-01.alias-tab` — alias-tab: keep attached. Place in the encounter’s named interaction zone with the clue reference visible from the same close view. Use the operation and obstruction described in action steps; do not substitute a decorative prop. Variants: idle, focused, blocked-with-reason, stable-after-action. Fallback: Labelled procedural proxy with the same shape/symbol and focus control; never remove its gameplay input..
+- `orison.design.sh-01.clue-panel` — Required clue close-up: Each fragment has a unique torn edge and matching record seal. The resulting pairs identify June Arlen, Tomas Reed, Ada Wren and Niko Bell; names alone are not the matching key. Variants: unexamined, exposed, recorded. Fallback: Readable diagram and faithful caption containing the same evidence..
+- `orison.design.sh-01.feedback` — Cue sheet: an invalid action gives the specified wrong-attempt response; each accepted step gives its stated physical result. Final result: names-first-four recorded from four corroborated pairs; no additional children invented. Variants: accepted-step, blocked-step, completed. Fallback: Caption and stable state marker for every audible cue..
+
+## Implementation task pack
+
+Task IM-SH-01; owner unassigned; status specified, implementation queued. Location boundary: src/kits/locations/school-hall/content, assets and sequences. Investigation owns mechanical progress and discovered evidence; Inventory owns items; Narrative owns choices/relationships; Campaign and Scene keep their existing completion/travel boundaries. Presentation owns control and cue descriptors. Dependencies: CAP-INPUT, CAP-MECHANISM, CAP-PROJECTION, CAP-SAVE and CAP-SEQUENCE. Physical controls and new logical state are proposed capabilities; current orisonOperations supports only observe/combine/use/dialogue/choose/solve/complete. Do not call new operation names or bypass source prerequisite checks as if they were installed.
+
+1. Read SH-01 and its source mapping. Load the actual school-hall incoming fixture; record current required clues and departure guard.
+2. Create the declared control definitions for photo-pieces, seal-view, alias-tab only after the shared input and state capabilities pass their tasks.
+3. Bind each exact action step to a validated Investigation transition. Place required clues in the authored scene before their observation receipts are possible.
+4. Project the accepted and blocked state changes through Presentation; use the listed procedural fallbacks until approved source assets exist.
+5. Coordinate finite completion via verified receipt waits; keep pressure inside Threat and do not put frame callbacks in a location Sequence.
+6. Commit existing source effects at the specified stage; preserve idempotency across reward, primary completion and departure.
+7. Implement the named restore and cancellation cases, then run the encounter and route acceptance walkthroughs from legal input.
+8. Attach source revision, observed behavior, screenshots and outstanding assets. Mark implemented only after these runtime gates pass.
+
